 ## Overview
-MultiPlaneNeRF is a radiance field optimization method that replaces the trainable, object-specific neural network weights of vanilla NeRF with a non-trainable 2D image-based representation [S1]. It solves the problems of long training times and poor generalization to unseen data by projecting 3D points onto a fixed set of 2D training images to create an aggregate feature vector, which is then processed by a small, shared implicit decoder [S1]. Unlike vanilla NeRF, which encodes shape and color in network weights requiring separate training per object, MultiPlaneNeRF allows a single decoder to generalize across many objects by simply swapping the input 2D images [S1].
+MultiPlaneNeRF is a radiance field representation that replaces the trainable volumetric encoding of vanilla NeRF with a non-trainable 2D image-based representation [S1]. It solves the problems of long training times and poor generalization to unseen data by projecting 3D points onto a fixed set of 2D images to create an aggregate feature vector, which is then processed by a small implicit decoder [S1]. Unlike vanilla NeRF, which encodes object shape and color in network weights requiring separate training per object, MultiPlaneNeRF allows a single decoder to generalize across many objects by simply swapping the input 2D images without retraining the network [S1].
 
